# Ali Therapy Admin — Coding Rules

## Before EVERY task (mandatory — do this first)

Never invent a new pattern. Before writing or changing code:

1. **Read the guide** — `lib/feature/FEATURE_FOLDER_GUIDE.md`
2. **Match folder structure** — copy an existing feature of the same type (`auth` for clean architecture; `all_employees` / `profile` for list→view; `reports` for grids)
3. **Match design / theme** — `AppColors`, `AppTextStyles`, `AppSizes`, `AppBackAppBar`, ScreenUtil (`.w` / `.h` / `.sp` / `.r`), shared widgets in `lib/core/widgets/`
4. **Match code design & flow** — `UI → Event → Bloc → UseCase → Repository → DataSource → State → UI`; navigation via `AppNavigation` + `extra`; loading via `AppLoadingOverlay` / `AppLoadingDialog`
5. **Copy, then adapt** — open a similar working screen/file and follow it; do not redesign folders, AppBars, cards, or API wiring style

If unsure which file to copy, prefer the closest existing feature over creating something new.

## Must follow every time

1. **Beginner-friendly code**
   - Write simple, readable Dart/Flutter code.
   - Add clear comments in **English only** (no Roman Urdu).
   - Prefer short helpers and named constants over magic strings/numbers.

2. **Follow existing folder structure (locked — do not invent a new one)**
   - Shared code → `lib/core/` (`errors`, `network`, `routes`, `services`, `theme`, `utils`, `di`, `datasources`, `usecase`, `widgets`)
   - Shared reusable UI (across features) → `lib/core/widgets/` (example: `AppTextField`, `AppFieldLabel`)
   - Datasources → `lib/core/datasources/<feature_name>/` (contract + Dio impl)
   - Feature code:
     - Shared (both) → `lib/feature/<feature_name>/` — e.g. `auth`, `home`, `splash`, `reports`
     - Employee only → `lib/feature/employee/<feature_name>/` — e.g. `all_employees`, `profile`
     - Patient only → `lib/feature/patient/<feature_name>/` — e.g. `all_patients`, `patient_detail`, …
   - **Clean architecture (auth is the template — copy this every time):**
     ```
     lib/feature/<area>/<feature_name>/
       data/
         <use_case>_data/
           models/              # JSON → Dart (extends Entity)
           repositories/        # impl — calls core/datasources
       domain/
         <use_case>_domain/
           entities/            # pure business objects (no Dio/JSON)
           repositories/        # abstract contract only
           usecases/            # one class = one job
       presentation/
         bloc/
           <use_case>_bloc/     # *_bloc.dart + event + state (part files)
         pages/
           <screen_name>/
             <screen_name>_page.dart
         widgets/
           form/ | other/ | sections/
     ```
   - One API job / screen flow → its own `<use_case>_data` + `<use_case>_domain` + `<use_case>_bloc` (see auth: `login_*`, `forget_password_*`, `change_password_*`).
   - Full beginner guide: `lib/feature/FEATURE_FOLDER_GUIDE.md`
   - DI → `lib/injection.dart` + `lib/core/di/` (one module file each)
   - **Do not register stub blocs/repos in DI** until the API is wired (UI-first stays sample data).

3. **Presentation layout (locked — use for every new feature)**
   Reference features: `auth`, `home`, `reports`, `edit_employee`, `patient_detail`, `profile`.
   ```
   lib/feature/<area>/<feature_name>/
     presentation/
       pages/                              # full screen only
         <screen_name>/                    # one folder per screen (mandatory)
           <screen_name>_page.dart         # Scaffold + AppBar + SafeArea + content
           <screen_name>_detail_page.dart  # optional — keep detail with parent screen
       widgets/
         form/                             # shared form pieces (header, footer, date, file, row…)
         other/                            # shared feature widgets (cards, menus, rows…)
         sections/<section_name>/          # one folder per section (when needed)
           <section>_section.dart
           <section>_form_fields.dart
   ```
   - **Pages folders (mandatory for new screens):** never put `*_page.dart` flat under `pages/`. Always `pages/<screen_name>/<screen_name>_page.dart`.
   - If a screen has a detail page, put both in the **same** folder (e.g. `pages/package_attendance/package_attendance_page.dart` + `package_attendance_detail_page.dart`).
   - Separate screens get separate folders (e.g. `add_document/`, `add_education/` — not under `profile/`).
   - Scaffold / screens ALWAYS in `pages/` — never in widgets.
   - Put screen content **directly in the page** — never create a page-level `*_body.dart`.
   - Keep smaller reusable pieces (cards, fields, sections) in `widgets/`.
   - One widget = one file. Never pack multiple widgets in one file.
   - NEVER create private `_MyWidget` classes inside a page file.
   - **Expandable cards:** use `AppExpandableCard` **only** when card content is taller than the minimum collapsed height (long report / detail cards). Short normal cards stay plain — no See all / See less.
   - When expandable is used: first tall card on a screen → `initiallyExpanded: true`; remaining stay collapsed.
   - Do **not** invent a new folder layout for new features — copy auth / this pattern.

4. **Never ship incomplete or messy work**
   - No empty stubs that break the app.
   - No half-wired routes, missing imports, or broken `main.dart`.
   - Run / fix analyze issues for files you touch.

5. **Always use Flutter ScreenUtil for UI**
   - Import `package:flutter_screenutil/flutter_screenutil.dart` in every UI file.
   - Use `.w` / `.h` / `.sp` / `.r` — never hardcode raw pixel sizes.

6. **SafeArea + theme + shared inputs (strict)**
   - Wrap every screen `body` with `SafeArea`.
   - Text: always `AppTextStyles.*` — never inline `TextStyle(fontSize/fontWeight)`.
   - Icons: always `AppSizes.iconSm/Md/Lg/Xl`.
   - Text inputs: always `AppTextField` — never raw `TextField` / `TextFormField`.

7. **Shared AppBar (LOCKED — same look everywhere)**
   - Screens with back: always `AppBackAppBar` (`lib/core/widgets/app_back_app_bar.dart`) or `FormBackAppBar` alias.
   - Light background, centered teal title (`AppTextStyles.appBarTitle`), teal back/actions icons, no elevation.
   - Do NOT invent a custom AppBar per screen (no solid primary bar).
   - Dashboard uses `DashboardAppBar` with the **same** colors/title style (no back).
   - Report screens: `AppBackAppBar` + `AppSearchFilterSection` (search + filter button row; panel toggles below).

8. **UI-only first when requested**
   - Do not mix UI with logic / state management.
   - Do not use `setState`, Cubit, Bloc, Provider, or GetX for new form screens unless the user asks.
   - Wire actions later when requested.

9. **UI ↔ Bloc separation (LOCKED — always)**
   - UI may only: show widgets, dispatch **events**, listen to **states**.
   - UI must NEVER call UseCase, Repository, DataSource, or Dio directly.
   - Flow: `UI → Event → Bloc → UseCase → Repository → DataSource → State → UI`
   - Loading / error / success = Bloc **states** (e.g. `AuthLoading`), not local `setState` + UseCase in the widget.
   - Navigation helpers (`AppNavigation`) = route only — no auth/business logic.
   - Example: logout button → `AuthLogoutRequested` → Bloc → `AuthUnauthenticated` → `goLogin`.

10. **Shared loading UI (LOCKED)**
   - Full-screen loading: always use `AppLoadingOverlay` or `AppLoadingDialog` from `lib/core/widgets/app_loading_dialog.dart`.
   - Do NOT invent a new spinner dialog per screen — same teal card everywhere.
   - Auth primary buttons have **no** button spinner — page overlay handles loading.

11. **Shared confirm dialog (LOCKED)**
   - Yes / No / Confirm / Continue / Delete prompts → `showAppConfirmDialog` (`lib/core/widgets/app_confirm_dialog.dart`).
   - Pass custom `title`, `message`, `cancelLabel`, `confirmLabel`, colors per screen.
   - Do NOT invent a new confirm dialog layout per feature.

## Locked UI flow (keep this — future updates must follow)

1. **List → detail**
   - List screens open detail via `AppNavigation` + `extra` (never hardcode paths).
   - Detail lives in the **same** `pages/<feature>/` folder as the list when it belongs to that feature
     (e.g. `patient_dues/` + `patient_dues_history_page`, `package_attendance/` + detail,
     `refer_by_report/` + `referred_patients_page`).
   - Detail screens use `FormBackAppBar` (or shared report AppBar) — avoid custom black headers.

2. **Shortcut grids (same height everywhere)**
   - Reports menu, patient Records tab, employee Profile menu: **2-column grid**,
     `childAspectRatio: 2.15`, spacing `6.w` / `6.h`, tile style like `ReportGridTile`
     (icon chip + centered title). Match that size — do not invent a new grid height.

3. **Cards**
   - Short cards (profile header, progress event rows, total visit cards, etc.): **plain** —
     no See all / See less.
   - Tall / dense cards (reports billing cards, long patient/employee list cards, etc.):
     `AppExpandableCard` only. First tall card → `initiallyExpanded: true`.

4. **Reports**
   - Open from home Quick Access → reports sheet; sheet stays open when pushing a report
     (do not pop sheet before navigate).
   - Shared pieces: `AppSearchFilterSection`, `report_filters_header`, filter field labels.
   - List/report search+filter layout (locked): one row = search field + filter button; filter panel opens below (same as All Employees / All Patients).

5. **Navigation animation**
   - Every route: `pageBuilder` + `AppPage.slide(state, child)`.

6. **UI-first**
   - Ship UI with sample data first; wire APIs / Cubit later when asked.

When updating UI later: **copy an existing screen of the same type** — do not invent a new pattern.

## Dependency Injection

- Shared DI in `lib/core/di/` — **one file per module**.
- Entry: `lib/injection.dart` → `setupCoreDi()`.
- New feature DI → new module file, then register in `di_setup.dart`.
